 ],
 "literal": "Like seeing the rising moon in the sea, / the lord of the land of lofty mountains with gushing white waterfalls, / is like the sun, O friend! / My large, bamboo-like shoulders are like the puncture-vine flower.",
 "translation": "Like seeing the rising moon over the ocean is the lord of the lofty mountains where white waterfalls gush. He is like the sun, my friend, and my large, bamboo-like shoulders are like the puncture-vine flower.",
 "modern": "அலைகள் வீசும் கடலில் உதிக்கின்ற முழு நிலவைக் காண்பது போல, வெள்ளிய அருவிகள் கொட்டுகின்ற உயர்ந்த மலைநாட்டை உடைய தலைவன் விளங்குகிறான். தோழியே! அவன் சூரியனைப் போன்றவன்; என்னுடைய பெரிய மூங்கில் போன்ற தோள்களோ சூரியனை நோக்கித் திரியும் நெருஞ்சிப் பூவைப் போன்றன.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her close friend about her deep devotion to the hero. She compares the hero, who rules over the lofty mountains with gushing white waterfalls, to the sun. She compares her own beautiful, bamboo-like shoulders to the puncture-vine (neruñci) flower, which always turns its face to follow the sun. Just as the flower cannot exist without looking at the sun, her beauty and life depend entirely on him. The comparison of the hero to the rising moon over the sea highlights his cool, pleasing nature, while his role as the sun highlights her constant devotion.",
